# Which suites a changed path can affect. Read by board_suites (ci/board.sh).
#
#   <pattern>   <suite>[,<suite>...]    suites: cargo e2e resilience rust-vtn | all | -  (none)
#
# The first matching rule wins, so specific rules come first. A pattern with a '/' is a shell
# glob on the repo-relative path ('*' also matches '/'); a pattern without one matches top-level
# files only. A ticket runs the union over its changed paths; the last rule, '*', makes any path
# no rule names run everything. Write a rule only when you can name what the path cannot affect.
# The audits and the CI mechanism's own tests (ci/test_*.sh) run for every ticket regardless.
#
#   cargo       the VEN cargo tier (fmt, clippy, test, audits) of the quick tier
#   rust-vtn    run_all_tests.sh --rust      (the openleadr-rs submodule's own tests)
#   e2e         run_all_tests.sh --e2e       (behave over the whole stack, UIs included)
#   resilience  run_all_tests.sh --resilience

# Documentation and tooling no suite builds or runs
docs/*                          -
wiki/*                          -
openspec/*                      -
.claude/*                       -
# The merge gates and the host lock are used by the suites and the runner
ci/audits/*                     all
ci/locks/*                      all
ci/*                            -
*.md                            -

# The UIs are built and driven only by the E2E stack (browser steps)
VEN/ui/*                        e2e
VTN/ui/*                        e2e
lab-ui/*                        e2e

# Test harness files, by the suite whose compose file or script they belong to
tests/features/*                e2e
tests/failure_recovery_test.sh  resilience
tests/*openleadr-test*          rust-vtn
tests/*ven-unit-test*           cargo
tests/*ven-coverage*            cargo

# Rust code the stack runs: the cargo tier, the stack builds, the restart tests
VEN/*                           cargo,e2e,resilience
lab-core/*                      cargo,e2e,resilience
VTN/bff/*                       cargo,e2e,resilience
VTN/*                           e2e,resilience

*                               all
